WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.380
We've kept business logic pure, and governance consistent.

2
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.190
Now, how do we test all of it

3
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.250
— without writing everything twice?

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.490
Same trick as always:

5
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.750
write the behaviour once, and choose where it runs.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.320
This is Gherkin.

7
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.980
It says what the service does

8
00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.070
— never how the request is sent.

9
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.510
That one property is why it can run at two levels.

10
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:25.510
One vocabulary.

11
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.030
Two step libraries.

12
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.400
Level one:

13
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.440
point the runner's glue at cucumber-utils.

14
00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.840
Spring MockMvc stands the service up in-process

15
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.830
— no server, no network.

16
00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.240
And the request goes through the

17
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.850
real Chenile controller and pipeline

18
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.740
— so security, tenancy and i18n run too.

19
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:46.800
Governance is under test.

20
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.180
Level two:

21
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.130
switch the glue to it-cucumber-utils from chenile-bdd,

22
00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.060
and deploy the service.

23
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.370
Same scenarios.

24
00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.340
But now, “I POST a REST request” is REST Assured,

25
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.940
hitting a real URL over HTTP.

26
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.820
Side by side, the step text is identical.

27
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.720
Only the engine changes:

28
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.240
MockMvc, or RestAssured.given().

29
00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.270
Swap the glue

30
00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.700
— not the spec.

31
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:15.930
Fast in-process tests on every build.

32
00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:18.650
Full REST Assured tests before release.

33
00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:19.830
One specification

34
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.940
— and it doubles as living documentation.

35
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.390
And it-cucumber-sec-utils does the same for secured endpoints.

36
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:30.380
Same philosophy as the whole series:

37
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.070
write it once, and decide placement by configuration.

38
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.620
Next episode:

39
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.240
messaging

40
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.770
— one interface, many transports.
